I've queued the #456 fix with the manager again; nothing has merged yet.

**Why it came back:** the last land wasn't red because of the code. Its build pipeline was cancelled before it ever started, so there was no verdict. Jody's earlier dependency-floor red was already fixed in the work I picked up.

**This run:**
- I recommitted the work on main `b35f308` as three commits:
  - `7655bc2d`: the fix. The Java state client now gives a queue or priority queue offer/consume/peek/size methods at parity with Go, instead of treating it as a singleton.
  - `46d31c42`: the follow-ups added to PROPOSALS.md.
  - `7d5ae2bd`: a statequeue fixture in the current-generation gate, so a gate now generates and compiles a state queue in every language. Its dependency pins meet main's floors.
- I started a build job (pipeline 3096982545), but no runner picked it up within 15 minutes, so it gave no verdict. The manager builds the land itself before merging.

**Not verified this run:**
- `go test ./scripts/` passes here.
- The new Java queue test, `statewrapper_queue_test.go`, needs generated protos and only runs in the build job.
- The statequeue fixture's Go, Java and Rust legs passed in an earlier run of this same change. The full current-generation gate has not been rerun with it since then.

**Left for the run after the manager's verdict:**
- If it merges: post the outcome comment (no service handlers were touched; looper-trace's only findings belong to #311), then close the issue.
- If it comes back red: fix it and land again.
- The backport PRs are already open: 2.0 #881 (v2.0.33), 2.1 #882 (v2.1.26), 2.2 #883 (v2.2.23), 2.3 #884 (v2.3.25), 2.4 #878 (v2.4.25), 2.5 #879 (v2.5.26) and 2.6 #880 (v2.6.14).
- There is no tag to cut on main, because `v2.6.2` already exists on release/2.6; 2.6's patch is #880's `v2.6.14`.
- Once this lands, #327 puts the queues back into its `proto-helpers` fixture.
